    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1267-a1">

                <pb facs="1146" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg888"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1—Telegram—Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Roosevelt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Commandant of the Naval Station at Guam</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maxwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 25, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The cable company informs the department as follows:</p>
                <p>A protest has been received by the company from the Japanese Government against
                    stoppage of a message which was written in plain Japanese language.</p>
                <p>You will forward immediately by cable to the department a translation of the
                    message referred to. 17025.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
